  "text": "```verilog\nmodule axis_adapter #\n(\n    parameter S_DATA_WIDTH = 8,\n    parameter S_KEEP_ENABLE = (S_DATA_WIDTH>8),\n    parameter S_KEEP_WIDTH = ((S_DATA_WIDTH+7)/8),\n    parameter M_DATA_WIDTH = 8,\n    parameter M_KEEP_ENABLE = (M_DATA_WIDTH>8),\n    parameter M_KEEP_WIDTH = ((M_DATA_WIDTH+7)/8),\n    parameter ID_ENABLE = 0,\n    parameter ID_WIDTH = 8,\n    parameter DEST_ENABLE = 0,\n    parameter DEST_WIDTH = 8,\n    parameter USER_ENABLE = 1,\n    parameter USER_WIDTH = 1\n)\n(\n    input  wire                     clk,\n    input  wire                     rst,\n    /*\n     * AXI input\n     */\n    input  wire [S_DATA_WIDTH-1:0]  s_axis_tdata,\n    input  wire [S_KEEP_WIDTH-1:0]  s_axis_tkeep,\n    input  wire                     s_axis_tvalid,\n    output wire                     s_axis_tready,\n    input  wire                     s_axis_tlast,\n    input  wire [ID_WIDTH-1:0]      s_axis_tid,\n    input  wire [DEST_WIDTH-1:0]    s_axis_tdest,\n    input  wire [USER_WIDTH-1:0]    s_axis_tuser,\n    /*\n     * AXI output\n     */\n    output wire [M_DATA_WIDTH-1:0]  m_axis_tdata,\n    output wire [M_KEEP_WIDTH-1:0]  m_axis_tkeep,\n    output wire                     m_axis_tvalid,\n    input  wire                     m_axis_tready,\n    output wire                     m_axis_tlast,\n    output wire [ID_WIDTH-1:0]      m_axis_tid,\n    output wire [DEST_WIDTH-1:0]    m_axis_tdest,\n    output wire [USER_WIDTH-1:0]    m_axis_tuser\n);\n\n    // Internal parameters\n    localparam S_BYTES = (S_DATA_WIDTH + 7) / 8;\n    localparam M_BYTES = (M_DATA_WIDTH + 7) / 8;\n    localparam S_BITS  = S_DATA_WIDTH;\n    localparam M_BITS  = M_DATA_WIDTH;\n\n    // State machine states\n    localparam ST_IDLE = 2'd0;\n    localparam ST_PROC = 2'd1;\n    localparam ST_DONE = 2'd2;\n\n    // Registers\n    reg [1:0] state;\n    reg [S_BITS-1:0] s_data_reg;\n    reg [S_KEEP_WIDTH-1:0] s_keep_reg;\n    reg s_last_reg;\n    reg [ID_WIDTH-1:0] s_tid_reg;\n    reg [DEST_WIDTH-1:0] s_tdest_reg;\n    reg [USER_WIDTH-1:0] s_tuser_reg;\n\n    // Output registers\n    reg [M_BITS-1:0] m_data_reg;\n    reg [M_KEEP_WIDTH-1:0] m_keep_reg;\n    reg m_last_reg;\n    reg [ID_WIDTH-1:0] m_tid_reg;\n    reg [DEST_WIDTH-1:0] m_tdest_reg;\n    reg [USER_WIDTH-1:0] m_tuser_reg;\n    reg m_valid_reg;\n\n    // Byte offset tracking\n    // For S_DATA_WIDTH > M_DATA_WIDTH: we need to track which byte of the source we're at\n    // For S_DATA_WIDTH < M_DATA_WIDTH: we need to accumulate bytes\n    // For equal widths: direct pass-through\n\n    // Let's use a general approach with byte-level FIFO-like buffer\n    // We'll track the number of valid bytes in the current source beat and the byte offset\n\n    // Number of valid bytes in current source beat\n    reg [3:0] s_valid_bytes;\n    // Byte offset within current source beat (0 to S_BYTES-1)\n    reg [3:0] s_byte_offset;\n    // For accumulation when M > S: number of bytes accumulated in output buffer\n    reg [3:0] m_accum_bytes;\n    // Output buffer for accumulation\n    reg [M_BITS-1:0] m_accum_data;\n    reg [M_KEEP_WIDTH-1:0] m_accum_keep;\n\n    // Helper: count valid bytes from tkeep\n    function [3:0] count_bytes;\n        input [S_KEEP_WIDTH-1:0] keep;\n        integer i;\n        begin\n            count_bytes = 0;\n            for (i = 0; i < S_KEEP_WIDTH; i = i + 1) begin\n                count_bytes = count_bytes + keep[i];\n            end\n        end\n    endfunction\n\n    // Helper: extract byte from source data\n    function [7:0] get_s_byte;\n        input [S_BITS-1:0] data;\n        input [3:0] byte_idx;\n        begin\n            get_s_byte = data[byte_idx*8 +: 8];\n        end\n    endfunction\n\n    // Helper: set byte in output data\n    function [M_BITS-1:0] set_m_byte;\n        input [M_BITS-1:0] data;\n        input [3:0] byte_idx;\n        input [7:0] byte_val;\n        begin\n            set_m_byte = data;\n            set_m_byte[byte_idx*8 +: 8] = byte_val;\n        end\n    endfunction\n\n    // Helper: set keep bit\n    function [M_KEEP_WIDTH-1:0] set_m_keep;\n        input [M_KEEP_WIDTH-1:0] keep;\n        input [3:0] byte_idx;\n        input enable;\n        begin\n            set_m_keep = keep;\n            if (enable)\n                set_m_keep[byte_idx] = 1'b1;\n            else\n                set_m_keep[byte_idx] = 1'b0;\n        end\n    endfunction\n\n    // Determine if we can accept new source data\n    wire s_ready = (state == ST_IDLE) && !m_valid_reg;\n\n    // Determine if we can output\n    wire m_fire = m_valid_reg && m_axis_tready;\n\n    // Determine if we're done with current source beat\n    wire s_beat_done = (s_byte_offset >= s_valid_bytes - 1);\n\n    // Determine if we need to accumulate (M > S case)\n    wire need_accumulate = (M_BYTES > S_BYTES);\n    // Determine if we need to split (S > M case)\n    wire need_split = (S_BYTES > M_BYTES);\n    // Equal width\n    wire equal_width = (S_BYTES == M_BYTES);\n\n    // For equal width, direct mapping\n    // For S > M: split source into multiple output beats\n    // For S < M: accumulate multiple source beats into one output beat\n\n    // Let's use a simpler approach:\n    // Maintain a byte-level buffer. On each cycle, if we can accept source data,\n    // load it. Then try to output as many bytes as fit in M_DATA_WIDTH.\n\n    // Actually, let's use a different approach with explicit state handling.\n\n    // For simplicity and correctness, let's handle the three cases:\n    // 1. Equal width: direct pass-through\n    // 2. S > M: split\n    // 3. S < M: accumulate\n\n    // Let's use a unified approach with a byte buffer.\n\n    // Buffer: stores up to max(S_BYTES, M_BYTES) bytes\n    localparam BUF_BYTES = (S_BYTES > M_BYTES) ? S_BYTES : M_BYTES;\n    localparam BUF_BITS = BUF_BYTES * 8;\n\n    reg [BUF_BITS-1:0] buf_data;\n    reg [BUF_BYTES-1:0] buf_valid;\n    reg [3:0] buf_count; // number of valid bytes in buffer\n    reg [3:0] buf_offset; // next byte to read from buffer\n\n    // Sideband for current packet\n    reg [ID_WIDTH-1:0] pkt_tid;\n    reg [DEST_WIDTH-1:0] pkt_tdest;\n    reg [USER_WIDTH-1:0] pkt_tuser;\n    reg pkt_last_pending;\n    reg pkt_last_byte_idx; // which byte index in the source beat has tlast\n\n    // State\n    reg [1:0] fsm_state;\n    localparam FSM_IDLE = 2'd0;\n    localparam FSM_LOAD = 2'd1;\n    localparam FSM_EMIT = 2'd2;\n\n    // Output\n    assign s_axis_tready = (fsm_state == FSM_IDLE) && !m_valid_reg;\n    assign m_axis_tvalid = m_valid_reg;\n    assign m_axis_tdata = m_data_reg;\n    assign m_axis_tkeep = m_keep_reg;\n    assign m_axis_tlast = m_last_reg;\n    assign m_axis_tid = m_tid_reg;\n    assign m_axis_tdest = m_tdest_reg;\n    assign m_axis_tuser = m_tuser_reg;\n\n    // Count valid bytes in source beat\n    wire [3:0] s_valid_bytes_wire = count_bytes(s_axis_tkeep);\n\n    // Determine if tlast byte is the last valid byte\n    // tlast indicates the last beat of a packet, not necessarily the last byte\n    // We need to track when we've emitted all bytes of the beat with tlast\n\n    // Let's simplify: we'll process byte by byte.\n    // When we load a source beat, we store all valid bytes in the buffer.\n    // We also store which byte index corresponds to tlast (if any).\n    // When emitting, we check if the current byte is the tlast byte.\n\n    // For tlast: it applies to the beat, so the last valid byte of that beat is the tlast byte.\n    // Actually, tlast is a per-beat signal. The beat with tlast=1 is the last beat of the packet.\n    // All bytes in that beat are part of the packet, and the beat is the last one.\n    // So when we emit the last byte of the tlast beat, we set m_axis_tlast.\n\n    // Let's track: is the current source beat a tlast beat?\n    reg s_is_tlast_beat;\n    reg [3:0] s_tlast_beat_valid_bytes;\n\n    // FSM\n    always @(posedge clk or posedge rst) begin\n        if (rst) begin\n            fsm_state <= FSM_IDLE;\n            m_valid_reg <= 1'b0;\n            m_data_reg <= {M_BITS{1'b0}};\n            m_keep_reg <= {M_KEEP_WIDTH{1'b0}};\n            m_last_reg <= 1'b0;\n            m_tid_reg <= {ID_WIDTH{1'b0}};\n            m_tdest_reg <= {DEST_WIDTH{1'b0}};\n            m_tuser_reg <= {USER_WIDTH{1'b0}};\n            buf_data <= {BUF_BITS{1'b0}};\n            buf_valid <= {BUF_BYTES{1'b0}};\n            buf_count <= 4'd0;\n            buf_offset <= 4'd0;\n            pkt_tid <= {ID_WIDTH{1'b0}};\n            pkt_tdest <= {DEST_WIDTH{1'b0}};\n            pkt_tuser <= {USER_WIDTH{1'b0}};\n            s_is_tlast_beat <= 1'b0;\n            s_tlast_beat_valid_bytes <= 4'd0;\n        end else begin\n            case (fsm_state)\n                FSM_IDLE: begin\n                    if (s_axis_tvalid && s_axis_tready) begin\n                        // Load source beat into buffer\n                        buf_count <= s_valid_bytes_wire;\n                        buf_offset <= 4'd0;\n                        s_is_tlast_beat <= s_axis_tlast;\n                        s_tlast_beat_valid_bytes <= s_valid_bytes_wire;\n                        pkt_tid <= s_axis_tid;\n                        pkt_tdest <= s_axis_tdest;\n                        pkt_tuser <= s_axis_tuser;\n\n                        // Load valid bytes into buffer\n                        for (integer i = 0; i < S_KEEP_WIDTH; i = i + 1) begin\n                            if (s_axis_tkeep[i]) begin\n                                buf_data[i*8 +: 8] <= s_axis_tdata[i*8 +: 8];\n                                buf_valid[i] <= 1'b1;\n                            end else begin\n                                buf_valid[i] <= 1'b0;\n                            end\n                        end\n                        // Clear remaining buffer bytes\n                        for (integer i = S_KEEP_WIDTH; i < BUF_BYTES; i = i + 1) begin\n                            buf_valid[i] <= 1'b0;\n                        end\n\n                        fsm_state <= FSM_EMIT;\n                    end\n                end\n\n                FSM_EMIT: begin\n                    if (m_valid_reg && m_axis_tready) begin\n                        // Output accepted, clear valid\n                        m_valid_reg <= 1'b0;\n\n                        // Check if we've emitted all bytes of current beat\n                        if (buf_offset >= buf_count - 1) begin\n                            // Done with this beat\n                            if (s_is_tlast_beat) begin\n                                // Packet complete, go to idle\n                                fsm_state <= FSM_IDLE;\n                            end else begin\n                                // More beats may come\n                                fsm_state <= FSM_IDLE;\n                            end\n                        end else begin\n                            // More bytes to emit from this beat\n                            buf_offset <= buf_offset + 1;\n                            // Prepare next output\n                            emit_next_byte;\n                        end\n                    end else if (!m_valid_reg) begin\n                        // No output pending, prepare next\n                        if (buf_offset < buf_count) begin\n                            emit_next_byte;\n                            m_valid_reg <= 1'b1;\n                        end else begin\n                            // Should not happen if logic is correct\n                            fsm_state <= FSM_IDLE;\n                        end\n                    end\n                end\n\n                default: begin\n                    fsm_state <= FSM_IDLE;\n                end\n            endcase\n        end\n    end\n\n    // Task to prepare next output byte\n    task emit_next_byte;\n        integer i;\n        reg [3:0] next_offset;\n        reg [7:0] byte_val;\n        reg [M_BITS-1:0] next_data;\n        reg [M_KEEP_WIDTH-1:0] next_keep;\n        reg next_last;\n        begin\n            next_offset = buf_offset;\n            next_data = {M_BITS{1'b0}};\n            next_keep = {M_KEEP_WIDTH{1'b0}};\n            next_last = 1'b0;\n\n            // Fill output with as many bytes as possible\n            for (i = 0; i < M_BYTES; i = i + 1) begin\n                if (next_offset + i < buf_count) begin\n                    byte_val = buf_data[(next_offset + i)*8 +: 8];\n                    next_data = set_m_byte(next_data, i, byte_val);\n                    next_keep = set_m_keep(next_keep, i, 1'b1);\n                end else begin\n                    next_keep = set_m_keep(next_keep, i, 1'b0);\n                end\n            end\n\n            // Check if last byte of this output is the tlast byte\n            // The tlast byte is the last valid byte of the tlast beat\n            // If s_is_tlast_beat and we're emitting the last byte of the beat\n            if (s_is_tlast_beat && (next_offset + M_BYTES - 1 >= buf_count - 1)) begin\n                // We're emitting the last byte of the tlast beat\n                // But only if the last byte we're emitting is actually the last byte of the beat\n                // The last byte of the beat is at index buf_count - 1\n                // We're emitting bytes from next_offset to next_offset + M_BYTES - 1\n                // If next_offset + M_BYTES - 1 >= buf_count - 1, we include the last byte\n                // But we need to check if the last byte we emit is the tlast byte\n                // The tlast byte is the last valid byte, which is at buf_count - 1\n                // If we're emitting buf_count - 1 in this output, then this output has tlast\n                if (next_offset + M_BYTES - 1 >= buf_count - 1) begin\n                    next_last = 1'b1;\n                end\n            end\n\n            m_data_reg <= next_data;\n            m_keep_reg <= next_keep;\n            m_last_reg <= next_last;\n            m_tid_reg <= pkt_tid;\n            m_tdest_reg <= pkt_tdest;\n            m_tuser_reg <= pkt_tuser;\n        end\n    endtask\n\nendmodule\n```<|im_end|>",
